WHAT THIS BUILD ADDS OVER 1.9.16
  `selfGrant` no longer treats "I could not read the list" as "the list is empty".  It calls
  `readGrantsOrNull`, and a failed read is refused with the errno carried into the log line
  (`why=...`).  Why that is a safety fix and not cosmetics: in 1.9.16 the boot path read the list as
  empty (it logged `added`) and was about to write back a one-entry list -- the owner's Shizuku/snub
  entries survived only because the unlink also failed at that moment.  Same build also carries the
  full-64-byte modprobe_path restore and the four-way gate entry points from 1.9.16.
  Boot reading from this package, before and after: `self-grant uid=10151 resealed saved=true
  list=[10151, 10133, 10135] why=-`, then `window PROVEN through the alias: "/sbin/modprobe" -> "/zz"`,
  `restore witnessed`, only then `sugate7 patch: rc=0 (NOP at 0x323400)`, then `app-exec su: execve
  allowed`.  One needle this boot, spent by the boot trigger itself, no adb-side writes involved.

WHY THE BOOT PATH NOW READS ITS OWN LIST AT ALL (mechanism, measured as a single-factor A/B over two
  boots -- ledger 677): the previous boot's file was the inode the harness created with `mv` as root
  (`u0_a151:root` + `app_data_file:s0`, missing the app's MLS categories), and an enforcing appdomain
  can neither read nor unlink it.  Restoring the app's own shape (`chown uid:gid` + `restorecon`) made
  the identical chain read three lines and reseal.  The harness is fixed to match: `drop_demo` rewrites
  in place (`cat >`, so inode/owner/label never change) and `seal_grants` restores the group and runs
  `restorecon`.  After a full 16-line run on this build the file still reads `u0_a151:u0_a151` +
  `app_data_file:s0:c512,c768`, 18 bytes, three lines.

BOUNDS AND LIMITS
  * Memory-only: bootloader never unlocked, no partition written, `adb reboot` restores the vendor name
    gate, removes /sbin/su and the daemon (criterion G measures exactly that).
  * One kernel needle per boot at most; the boot trigger does not re-fire on a boot already served
    (this boot logged `this boot already reads as escalated -- not firing the needle again` when the
    service was started again by hand, and that is the intended behaviour).
  * `job schedule rc=1` on this ROM: JobScheduler refuses the re-check job, so if relayd dies it is not
    re-armed by the scheduler -- it comes back when the app starts again or when 提权 is tapped.
  * A process that is already root is refused by the relay (`deny uid=0 cmd=SU 0 id`): the allow list
    covers app uids, and root does not need to be handed root.
  * The 6.0.1 route (`esc_sugate`) still keeps the older shape -- if its own enforce read is not
    available it patches and relies on the exec witness (clobber.c:898).  Unchanged here because this
    phone runs 7 and that branch cannot be witnessed on it.
  * Byte policy: every byte of this package has a reading from the boot above -- `classes.dex`,
    `lib/arm64-v8a/libesc.so` and `assets/broot7` are the freshly built ones that actually ran (cmp
    against tools/), unlike 1.9.16, which shipped 1.9.15's broot7 on purpose.

